# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cbdb-desktop-tests — environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and edit.  `.env` is gitignored: every path below is
# machine-specific.  Anything here can also be supplied as a real
# environment variable, which takes precedence over the file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# REQUIRED.  The CBDB-Desktop distribution under test (.zip or .7z).  This is
# the single input of the whole suite — every test runs against the binary,
# templates, Go sources and SQLite database staged out of this archive.
#
# Both container formats are read directly (py7zr for .7z), and a 7z that
# wraps the tree in a single top-level directory has that wrapper stripped,
# so either layout stages to the same shape.
CBDB_DESKTOP_ZIP=C:\Users\<you>\Dropbox\CBDB\CBDB Desktop\CBDB-Desktop_20260907.7z

# Where the archive is unpacked.  Defaults to <repo>/work.  Needs ~2 GB
# free; put it on a fast local disk (NOT inside Dropbox/OneDrive — the
# 1.2 GB CBDB.db would sync on every stage).
# CBDB_WORK_DIR=C:\cbdb-desktop-work

# Skip staging entirely and test an already-unpacked CBDB-Desktop tree.
# When set, it must be a directory containing Bin/, Data/, Templates/,
# Static/ and Code/.  CBDB_DESKTOP_ZIP is then only used for provenance.
# CBDB_APP_DIR=

# Seconds to wait for cbdb.exe to log its "CBDB server started: <url>" line.
# The first start on a cold file cache opens a 1.2 GB WAL database.
CBDB_STARTUP_TIMEOUT=180

# Seconds any single HTTP request to the app may take.  Some form queries
# (networks, group data) legitimately run for a minute on the full dataset.
CBDB_HTTP_TIMEOUT=300

# 1 = launch cbdb.exe with a PATH that cannot resolve rundll32, so its
# automatic "open the default browser" call fails harmlessly instead of
# spawning a browser window per test session.  Set to 0 to see the UI.
CBDB_SUPPRESS_BROWSER=1

# The table of outcomes that have been discussed and agreed to leave as
# they are for now.  Active here on purpose: the agreements are part of
# this repo (waivers.toml is committed), so a fresh checkout should judge
# the build the same way the maintainer does rather than reporting things
# he has already decided about.  Comment this line out to see the build
# with nothing tolerated.
#
# Each entry is keyed by a test function's own name -- plus, optionally,
# the parametrisation ids it applies to -- because that is the only
# address that survives a round started with no state: a defect id is
# assigned while one report is written and means nothing by the next.
# See tests/cbdb_desktop/waivers.py for the format and the modes.
#
# Unset means no waivers at all.  Set but missing or malformed stops the
# run rather than quietly waiving nothing.  A relative path resolves
# against the repo root.  Whatever a run waives is recorded in
# artifacts/waivers_applied.json and printed in both issue reports --
# nothing is tolerated invisibly.
CBDB_WAIVERS=waivers.toml
